"answer": "The emails regarding Project Zenith outline the project's lifecycle from initiation to ongoing updates. Project Zenith was announced in Q3 2023, led by Marcus Cole, with a kickoff on July 15th, aiming to optimize cloud storage solutions. Initial phases included gathering R&D ideas by July 20th to leverage AI for data visualization, followed by a design phase completion and the start of the development phase led by Omar Jensen. The team expanded by adding five members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, welcomed on September 10th. A significant budget approval of $2M was secured, though later adjusted to $550,000 due to unforeseen expenses to cover real-time analytics integration. Recent updates highlight a breakthrough in predictive analytics in Phase Two, with a detailed report scheduled for November 20th. Feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November, and security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption, are set to update in January."
